The ZEBRA protein (Zta, BZLF1) plays a critical role in the latency-to-lytic switch mechanism of Epstein-Barr Virus (EBV). As a transcription factor, it helps regulate the transition from the latent phase of viral infection to the lytic cycle by promoting the expression of genes necessary for virus replication. This process is essential for enabling EBV to induce immune responses while effectively managing its replication within the host.

